.TH DOTFILES-SYNC 1 "2026-10-29" "1.0.0" "dotfiles-watcher manual"
.SH NAME
dotfiles-sync \- stage, AI-commit, and push dotfiles bare repo changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dotfiles-sync
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dotfiles-sync
stages all changes to files tracked by the bare git repository at
.IR ~/.cfg/ ,
generates a concise commit message using
.BR gemini (1),
and pushes to
.IR origin/main .
Falls back to a timestamp commit message if
.B gemini
is unavailable or returns empty output.
.PP
Can be run manually at any time as well as being invoked automatically by
.BR dotfiles-watcher (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cfg/
Bare git repository.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/
Auto-scanned for new
.I *.service
and
.I *.timer
files to stage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dotfiles-watcher (1),
.BR git (1)
